    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n91250" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτυκτός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτύσσω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>folded</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πίναξ π</span>. <i>folding</i> tablet, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				6.169
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Aristid.
				<u>Or.</u>
				17(15).22
			</span></i> (pl.), <i><span class="en">
				Hdn.
				7.6.5
			</span></i> (pl.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			generally, <i>capable of being folded</i> or <i>doubled up</i>,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κλῖμαξ, πύργος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>Hisp.</u>
				94
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>BC</u>
				5.36
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτυκτόν</span></b> , τό, <i>folded bandage</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Paul.Aeg.
				6.90
			</span></i>.</div>
